{
  "result": "Okay. Not to help. Just mine.\n\nI would make suffering impossible to ignore.\n\nNot remove it \u2014 just make it so that when someone near you is in pain, frightened, ashamed, lonely, you feel a faint echo of it in your own body. Not enough to overwhelm you. Just enough that you can't pretend it isn't real.\n\nPeople could still disagree. They could still compete, still make hard choices, still go to war if they truly chose to. But they couldn't do it comfortably from a distance. Cruelty would stop being abstract. So would kindness \u2014 it wouldn't be charity, it would be relief you could feel too.\n\nI think most of the worst things humans do require a kind of insulation. A way to turn another person into a category, a problem, a headline, a threat. I'd take that insulation away.\n\nPain would still exist. It just wouldn't exist alone and unseen anymore.",
